  "text": ">{@cyd}\n\n1. Consider the pentagon $ABCDE$ and the point $F$ on side $AB$.\n2. Since $\\angle FAE=30^\\circ$, we can use trigonometry to find the length of segment $EF$.\n3. Since $AB=s$, we can use the law of cosines to find the length of segment $AE$.\n4. Using the law of sines, we can find the length of segment $EF$.\n5. Finally, we can simplify the expression for $EF$ in terms of $s$.\n\n@cyd\n></>.SuspendLayout();\n>\\#1\\left(m\\right)+\\#2\\left(poly\\right) $imer:\\ncn ordinal\\מת 문서称号\nat documents\\documentdefault.cs line 405\nat lambda(Slider AutoListItem0                              ---args);\n\n.anwser (waitangwa)\n\n {@cyd}\n step by step\n>Login information:\n\nMathematical knowledge\n\nBasic functions\nTrigonometric functions\nCosine law\nSine law\nRelationships\nIsosceles triangle\nEquilateral triangle\nNormal triangle\nUnique central channel\nAngular and normal elements\nIdentifying characteristics\nLong ophthalmic ray\nVariable center\nRay isochronous\nIdelodyne oval\nMinMax95 minimum value\nLength of the mean value\nAnkylogamy\nRational version\nBasic functions\n\nTrigonometric functions\n\nCosine law\n\nSine law\n\nRelationships\n\nIsosceles triangle\n\nEquilateral triangle\n\nNormal triangle\n\nUnique central channel\n\nAngular and normal elements\n\nIdentifying characteristics\n\nLong ophthalmic ray\n\nVariable center\n\nRay isochronous\n\nIdelodyne oval\n\nMinMax95 minimum value\n\nLength of the mean value\n\nAnkylogamy\n\nRational version\n\nThe student wants to know that in a regular pentagon, a point $ F $ is on side $ AB $, and $\\angle FAE=30^\\circ$, the length of segment $ EF $ in terms of the side length $ s $ of the pentagon.\n\nStep 1: Identify the triangle.\nTriangle $ FAE $ is a triangle in which $\\angle FAE=30^\\circ$.\n\nStep 2: Find the side length of triangle $ FAE $.\nIn a regular pentagon, the side length $ s $ and the radius of the circumscribed circle $ R $ are related. By the cosine law in triangle $ FAE $, we can find the length of side $ EF $.\n\nStep 3: Find the length of segment $ EF $.\nUsing the cosine law in triangle $ FAE $, we obtain:\n\n$ EF^2 = AE^2 + AF^2 - 2 \\cdot AE \\cdot AF \\cdot \\cos(\\angle FAE) $\n\n$ EF^2 = s^2 + s^2 - 2 \\cdot s \\cdot s \\cdot \\cos(30^\\circ) $\n\n$ EF^2 = 2s^2 - 2 \\cdot s^2 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} $\n\n$ EF^2 = 2s^2 - s^2\\sqrt{3} $\n\nStep 4: Simplify the expression for $ EF $.\nBy taking the square root of both sides of the equation and simplifying the expression, we find:\n\n$ EF = s \\cdot \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{3}} $\n\nanswered degrees mathgeek753 is\ne $\\begin{array}{r l c} \\text{Problem:}^{}\\ ! \\text{Find the length of}^{}\\underline{EF}^{}\\ \\text{in terms of}^{}^{}\\ m^{}\\text{that}^{}\\ \\olcancel{can}\\ \\overline[firstqrlc0*\\text{人}^{}\\{m8bc683*}\\{mic6bc683*\\}^{}{(サ}\\{3代683f\\}^{}\\text{point {$m$}}^{}\\{fs406ba0*}preserve其中}\\ \\{06523d6*}^{}\\text{have a }^{ ^{}Capabilities^{}}} ! \\end{array}$$slider.domsin.columnist\n\nA regular pentagon $ABCDE$ sides has a length $s$. Chos at a point $F$ on side $AB$, such that the degree $\\angle FAE$ equals $30\\degree$. Find the length $F$ with example segments in terms of $s$.\n\nจงหาความยาวด้านที่ตั้งแต่ตอน V 받 (Haasbo Cuscenti A dorrendtl?\n\n? answer:\n\n$$\\boxed{EF = s \\cdot \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{3}}}$$",
